# Odoo 18 Development Reference

## Context
This reference applies to Python modules developed in the ecosystem built on Odoo 18. You extends Odoo's functionality with specialized modules for social protection programs.

## Module Structure
The standard Odoo module structure in consists of these directories and files:

- `__init__.py` - Module entry point with imports
- `__manifest__.py` - Module descriptor with metadata
- `README.md` - Module documentation with installation and usage instructions
- `models/` - Business object definitions
- `views/` - XML view definitions
- `data/` - XML data files
- `security/` - Access controls and rules
- `wizards/` - Transient models
- `static/` - Static assets
- `controllers/` - HTTP controllers
- `reports/` - QWeb reports
- `tests/` - Test files for the module

## Python Coding Standards
Odoo 18 follows these Python coding patterns:

- 4 spaces for indentation, no tabs
- Maximum line length of 79 characters
- PEP 8 naming conventions:
  - `snake_case` for variables, methods, functions
  - `CamelCase` for classes
  - `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants
- Import ordering:
  1. Standard library imports
  2. Third-party imports
  3. Odoo imports
  4. Module imports (relative)

## Security Implementation
Security in Odoo modules uses these patterns:

- Access rights defined in CSV files (ir.model.access.csv)
- Record rules for complex security requirements
- Environment switching with `with self.env.su():` when required
- Input validation to prevent injection attacks
- HTML sanitization for display
- Sensitive data encryption

## Examples

Standard Odoo 18 module structure example:

```
addons/odoo_extension/
|-- __init__.py
|-- __manifest__.py
|-- models/
|   |-- __init__.py
|   |-- res_partner.py
|   |-- entitlement.py
|-- views/
|   |-- res_partner_views.xml
|   |-- entitlement_views.xml
|-- security/
|   |-- ir.model.access.csv
|   |-- security_rules.xml
|-- data/
|   |-- demo_data.xml
|-- static/
|   |-- description/
|   |-- src/
|-- tests/
|   |-- __init__.py
|   |-- test_partner.py
|   |-- test_entitlement.py
```

Non-standard module structure with pattern issues:

```
my_odoo_mod/
|-- main.py  # Non-standard entry point
|-- models.py  # All models in one file
|-- views.xml  # All views in one file
|-- demo.xml
```

## Documentation Patterns

Effective documentation in Odoo includes:

- Docstrings for all classes and methods
- Comments explaining complex business logic
- Updated README.md with installation and usage instructions
- Standard method ordering within model classes

